  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2020-05-13",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would raise the statutory upper limit used for specified supervisory levy amounts payable by authorised non-operating holding companies, as part of prudential regulator funding reforms.",
   "The limit would be $10 million for the financial year beginning 1 July 2020, with later limits indexed using the latest published Consumer Price Index figures.",
   "It would commence the day after royal assent and apply to levy determinations made from commencement, alongside separate bills covering other regulated sectors."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The statutory limit definition and related levy restrictions would be clarified.",
   "Indexation would compare the latest quarter with the same quarter a year earlier, then add 0.030.",
   "Only index numbers published by the Australian Statistician would be used."
  ],
  "affected": "Authorised non-operating holding companies liable for supervisory levies would be affected.",
